{"rank": 2410, "kind": "function", "entry": "run_blocks", "starter": "from typing import Any, Dict, List\n\n\nclass capture:\n    \"\"\"Context manager: suppress and record the listed exception types raised in its with block.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, *exc_types):\n        pass\n\n    def __enter__(self):\n        pass\n\n    def __exit__(self, exc_type, exc, tb):\n        pass\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Provided \u2014 keep this. The tests call run_blocks(types, blocks, reuse):\n#   each block is an exception name to raise inside `with capture(*types) as c:`, or \"ok\" to raise nothing.\n#   reuse=False: a fresh capture per block;  reuse=True: one capture object re-entered for every block.\n# For each block it reports what escaped the with statement and the capture's errors afterwards.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEXCEPTIONS = {cls.__name__: cls for cls in (\n    Exception, ValueError, KeyError, LookupError, IndexError, TypeError,\n    ZeroDivisionError, ArithmeticError, OSError, FileNotFoundError, RuntimeError)}\n\n\ndef _describe(err):\n    return f\"{type(err).__name__}: {err}\"\n\n\ndef run_blocks(types: List[str], blocks: List[str], reuse: bool) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    shared = capture(*(EXCEPTIONS[name] for name in types))\n    report = []\n    for i, block in enumerate(blocks):\n        manager = shared if reuse else capture(*(EXCEPTIONS[name] for name in types))\n        escaped = None\n        try:\n            with manager as c:\n                if c is not manager:\n                    raise AssertionError(\"__enter__ must return the capture object itself\")\n                if block != \"ok\":\n                    raise EXCEPTIONS[block](f\"block {i}\")\n        except AssertionError:\n            raise\n        except Exception as err:\n            escaped = _describe(err)\n        report.append({\"escaped\": escaped, \"errors\": [_describe(e) for e in manager.errors]})\n    return report\n", "compare": "exact", "notes": "Write capture as a class: __enter__ returns the capture itself, and errors starts as [] and records the exception objects (not their types). Subclasses of the listed types are caught too; capture() with no types suppresses nothing; re-entering the same capture keeps adding to errors. run_blocks is provided: it raises a named exception (or nothing) inside your with block and reports what escaped.", "tests": [{"args": [["ValueError"], ["ValueError"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": null, "errors": ["ValueError: block 0"]}], "hidden": false}, {"args": [["ValueError"], ["KeyError"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": "KeyError: 'block 0'", "errors": []}], "hidden": false}, {"args": [["ValueError", "KeyError"], ["ok", "KeyError", "TypeError"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": null, "errors": []}, {"escaped": null, "errors": ["KeyError: 'block 1'"]}, {"escaped": "TypeError: block 2", "errors": []}], "hidden": false}, {"args": [["ZeroDivisionError"], ["ok"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": null, "errors": []}], "hidden": true}, {"args": [[], ["ValueError", "ok"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": "ValueError: block 0", "errors": []}, {"escaped": null, "errors": []}], "hidden": true}, {"args": [["LookupError"], ["KeyError", "IndexError", "ValueError"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": null, "errors": ["KeyError: 'block 0'"]}, {"escaped": null, "errors": ["IndexError: block 1"]}, {"escaped": "ValueError: block 2", "errors": []}], "hidden": true}, {"args": [["ArithmeticError", "OSError"], ["ZeroDivisionError", "FileNotFoundError", "RuntimeError"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": null, "errors": ["ZeroDivisionError: block 0"]}, {"escaped": null, "errors": ["FileNotFoundError: block 1"]}, {"escaped": "RuntimeError: block 2", "errors": []}], "hidden": true}, {"args": [["Exception"], ["RuntimeError", "TypeError", "ok"], false], "expected": [{"escaped": null, "errors": ["RuntimeError: block